<title>USA: Varian to cut 115 workers.</title>
<headline>Varian to cut 115 workers.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Varian Associates Inc said Thursday it is reducing the work force at its semiconductor equipment factories in Gloucester, Mass., and Palo Alto, Calif., by some 115 workers due to slow demand.</p>
<p>The move trims employment at that business by about 6 percent and cuts total company employment by less than 2 percent.</p>
<p>Varian said the semiconductor industry continues to suffer from over capacity and price discounting, which leads to lower demand for new chip-making equipment.</p>
<p>About 85 of the positions affected are at the Gloucester plant, which had a similar reduction in mid-August, with the balance at the Palo Alto unit.</p>
<p>Varian said those affected will receive severance payments and outplacement assistance.</p>
<p>Shares of Varian were 3/8 lower at 47-3/4 in midday trading on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
